        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "This is already solid for a small CLI - `281` LOC (`main.go:1`, `remotes.go:1`, `selector.go:1`, `browser.go:1`), ships cross-platform, `mise` + `goreleaser` (`mise.toml:1`, `.goreleaser.yaml:1`). To signal senior/staff level, fix the gaps that reviewer would spot in 5 min:\n\n### 1. Correctness & Robustness - Biggest Gap\n\n*   **Fragile URL parsing** `remotes.go:43` - hand-rolled `strings.Index`/`IndexByte` breaks on `ssh://git@host:2222/owner/repo`, `git://`, `https://token@github.com/owner/repo.git`, `org/subgroup/repo`. Use `net/url` + explicit `git@host:` scp-like parser. You have only 3 test vectors `main_test.go:6` - add table-driven with subgroups, ports, `.git` stripping, trailing slashes.\n*   **`frontendURL` `remotes.go:63`** - `strings.Fields(repoPath)` swallow is a hack for spaces, `prefixes` map allocated per-call, missing `default` case returns `\"/owner/repo\"` silently if frontend typo. Make it `map[string]string` const + validate, return `(string,error)`.\n*   **No timeouts/cancellation** - `exec.Command(\"git\"...).Output()` `remotes.go:14`, `tmux display-message` `remotes.go:80`, `xdg-settings get` `browser.go:37` can hang indefinitely. Wrap with `context.WithTimeout(2s)`.\n*   **`repositoryPath` lowercases everything** `remotes.go:56` - correct for GitHub but breaks case-sensitive Gitea/Codeberg hosts. Only lowercase if needed.\n\n### 2. Architecture / Testability (`13.1%` coverage)\n\nAll in `package main`, untestable side-effects. Senior move: inject dependencies.\n\n```go\ntype runner interface { Output(ctx context.Context, name string, args ...string) ([]byte,error) }\ntype env interface { Getenv(string) string }\n```\n\nThen `gitRemotes`, `launchBrowser`, `selectItem` become unit-testable without `fzf`/`git` installed. Split into `internal/git`, `internal/browser`, `internal/selector`. `indexOf` `selector.go:53` returning `0` on miss hides bugs - should panic/error.\n\n### 3. Toolchain Drift - Free Wins\n\n*   `go.mod:3` says `go 1.22` but `mise.toml:3` is `1.27.0` and `README.md:31` says `1.26.6`. Bump `go.mod` and fix README - reviewer flags this as lack of ownership.\n*   `gofmt -l` only `mise.toml:17` - add `golangci-lint` + `staticcheck`. `go vet` `mise.toml:22` is not enough.\n*   `.gitignore:2` ignores `/open-repo` but binary `open-repo:3.0M` still on disk untracked - good, but `git ls-files` confirms not committed. Add `goreleaser` `archives` checksum verification step to `README.md:Verify`.\n\n### 4. CI / Release Quality\n\n`.github/workflows/release.yml:1` only runs on `tags` + `workflow_dispatch`. Missing PR CI:\n\n```yaml\non: [push, pull_request]\njobs: { check: { runs-on: ubuntu-latest, steps: [fmt-check, vet, test -cover -race, govulncheck] } }\n```\n\nNo `-race`, no `govulncheck`, no coverage threshold, no `actionlint`. Add `SBOM` + `cosign` signing to `goreleaser.yaml`.\n\n### 5. CLI Polish (Product Thinking)\n\n*   No `--help`, `--version` (injected via `ldflags` from git tag), `--dry-run`, `--remote`, `--frontend`, `--print-url` flags. Currently forces interactivity `main.go:31,40` - breaks scripting.\n*   `selector.go:17` `--prompt=` concatenates user input directly to `fzf` arg. Use `--prompt`, prompt` correctly but test escaping.\n*   `browser.go:11` hardcodes `omarchy-launch-browser` / `app.zen_browser.zen` / `flatpak` / `uwsm-app` - leaks personal env into public CLI. Abstract behind `$BROWSER` respect + documented config `~/.config/open-repo/config.toml`.\n\n### 6. Docs / Ownership\n\n*   Remove `open-repo`/`open-repo.exe` from working tree or document `mise run build` output to `dist/`.\n*   Add `CONTRIBUTING.md`, issue templates, `LICENSE` check (currently generic).\n*   Add `go test -coverprofile` badge and `mise run check` as pre-commit hook (`.github/hooks` only has `entire`).\n\n**Priority order if you want max signal/effort:**\n\n1.  Fix `go.mod`/`README.md` drift + add `golangci-lint` + PR `check` workflow (30min, high signal)\n2.  Rewrite `repositoryPath` with `net/url` + exhaustive tests, make `frontendURL` validated (1h, proves correctness)\n3.  Inject `exec`/`env` + add `-race`/`-cover` >80% (2h, proves test discipline)\n4.  Add flags `--help --version --dry-run --remote --frontend` via `cobra` or std `flag` (proves product thinking)\n\nWant me to implement 1-2 as a PR diff?\n",
